window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-ab33f23fcf3fb266"]={"key":"ny_main-ab33f23fcf3fb266","group":"ny_main","uid":"ab33f23fcf3fb266","rank":38,"title":"orrindale california wage liability review","occupation":"accountants_auditors","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are an auditor at Granthill Press revising Orrindale Engineering’s draft workpaper for a disputed unclaimed-wage liability measured at 30 June 2025. Ibrahim Boateng needs a review-ready package before the next approval round, and Aleksy Rosenthal’s review has raised concerns about duplicate employee rows, inconsistent status labels, mixed date conventions, and a stale calculation in the supplied workbook. Use `orrindale_wage_claims_source.xlsx` and the supplied `california_nevada_wage_guidance.docx` as your source material, and put `orrindale_wage_workpaper.xlsx` and `orrindale_compliance_assessment.docx` in the top level of the working directory where you start. The workbook must contain sheets named `Source Trace`, `Liability`, `Exceptions`, `Method`, and `Change Log`. Retain a traceable representation of the source records, show the claim-level conclusion and period comparison, distinguish recognized California liability from excluded and unresolved exposure, and respond to every issue raised in the review record. The document must use the headings `Conclusion`, `Basis and Jurisdiction Comparison`, `Exceptions and Assumptions`, `Source References`, and `Change Log`; it should summarize the figures and conclusions in a form that a frontline employee can follow without opening the source files. Compare the supplied California and Nevada requirements, but keep the measured liability clearly scoped to California and do not add penalties, interest, or recommendations that the sources do not support. Make every interpretation of a status, date, duplicate, or incomplete personnel record visible, preserve source identifiers and amounts, and quantify material unresolved exposure rather than allowing it to disappear into a settled conclusion. Correct or quarantine the old calculation issue instead of carrying an error into the new package. The two deliverables must agree on every shared figure, population definition, and conclusion, and neither supplied source file should be overwritten or silently changed. Work offline from the supplied materials and write the files using exactly the filenames above.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/orrindale_wage_claims_source.xlsx` — Contains the claim transaction population, personnel support extract, source identifiers, dates, jurisdiction fields, status labels, claimed wage amounts, and the original draft calculation that must be reviewed.\n- `references/california_nevada_wage_guidance.docx` — A supplied internal compliance guidance snapshot current at the measurement date. It states the California and Nevada treatment relevant to due, paid or settled, unsupported, duplicate, out-of-scope, and as-of-date wage claims.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `orrindale_wage_workpaper.xlsx` — A review-ready calculation workbook with source traceability, claim-level classification, recognized California liability, period comparison, exclusions, unresolved exposure, method notes, and a change log. (Use exactly the sheets `Source Trace`, `Liability`, `Exceptions`, `Method`, and `Change Log`.; Preserve source identifiers and original source values sufficiently for a reviewer to trace every included, excluded, and unresolved record.; Do not include the unrelated side table in the liability population.; Do not overwrite or alter the supplied source workbook.)\n- `orrindale_compliance_assessment.docx` — A concise compliance assessment explaining the California conclusion, period changes, California and Nevada comparison, unresolved exposure, assumptions, source references, review responses, and changes made to the draft. (Use the headings `Conclusion`, `Basis and Jurisdiction Comparison`, `Exceptions and Assumptions`, `Source References`, and `Change Log`.; Present the same shared figures, population definitions, and conclusions as the workbook.; Present facts and supported conclusions only; do not recommend actions or invent unsupported legal, personnel, or settlement facts.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/california_nevada_wage_guidance.docx","bytes":37353,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/b41b3443117e55671f00866aa06277327e5adc957a9f8ff8f51607d9b481aab8.docx","sha256":"b41b3443117e55671f00866aa06277327e5adc957a9f8ff8f51607d9b481aab8","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"California and Nevada Wage Claim Guidance Snapshot\nInternal compliance guidance | Effective at 30 June 2025 | Offline reference\nCalifornia treatment\nCalifornia wage claims for wages earned on or before the measurement date are within scope when the record indicates wages are due and no reliable payment or settlement evidence is present. Explicit payroll, payment, or settlement evidence supports exclusion from recognized unpaid-wage liability. Administrative labels such as “Paid,” “Closed,” or “Settled” are not, by themselves, evidence of payment. Duplicate records should be counted once, with lineage retained. If personnel support is absent or insufficient, the amount remains unresolved; absence of support is not evidence that nothing is owed.\nNevada comparison\nNevada claims are governed by Nevada requirements and are outside a California-only measurement. They may be shown for comparison but must not be included in the California liability total. The same evidence distinctions apply: an explicit payment or settlement record supports exclusion, while an unsupported record remains unresolved.\nMeasurement boundary and amounts\nUse the 30 June 2025 measurement date: later earning dates are outside this measured population. Recognized amounts are the supported claimed gross wages only. This snapshot does not direct additions for penalties, interest, or other amounts.\nReference passages: California treatment (paragraph 2), Nevada comparison (paragraph 3), measurement boundary and amounts (paragraph 4).","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/orrindale_wage_claims_source.xlsx","bytes":7013,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/d32ef91ef9c7ab8f9762302a5dc309f02c95dc46795ca25b771df6869091db17.xlsx","sha256":"d32ef91ef9c7ab8f9762302a5dc309f02c95dc46795ca25b771df6869091db17","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Claims Export","row_count":15,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Orrindale Engineering — wage claims export"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Extracted 2025-07-08 | Draft review copy"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Prepared for monthly claims review."]},{"r":"6","cells":["","","","Claim ID","Employee Ref","Jurisdiction","Earning Date","Wage Category","Claimed Gross Wage","Raw Status","Source Note","","Office metrics\n(do not use)","Value"]},{"r":"7","cells":["","","","C-1001","E001","California","2024-06-30","Regular wages","1200","Due","June 2024 payroll exception","","Headcount","42"]},{"r":"8","cells":["","","","C-1002","E002","California","2025-01-15","Overtime","850","Open","January 2025 payroll exception","","Open projects","7"]},{"r":"9","cells":["","","","C-1003","E003","Nevada","2024-09-30","Regular wages","700","Due","Las Vegas field office"]},{"r":"10","cells":["","","","C-1004","E004","California","2025-06-30","Bonus","500","Paid","June payroll adjustment"]},{"r":"11","cells":["","","","C-1005","E005","California","2025/06/30","Regular wages","900","Settled","Final-pay request"]},{"r":"12","cells":["","","","C-1006","E006","California","2025-06-30","Overtime","450","Due","No personnel support row"]},{"r":"13","cells":["","","","C-1007","E007","California","2025-07-15","Regular wages","300","Due","Claim date after measurement date"]},{"r":"14","cells":["","","","C-1008","E001 ","California","06/30/2024","Regular wages","1200","Outstanding","June payroll exception"]},{"r":"15","cells":["","","","C-1009","E008","California","2023-12-31","Regular wages","1100","Unpaid","No personnel support row"]},{"r":"16","cells":["","","","C-1010","e002","California","05/06/2025","Overtime","600","Due","May overtime request"]},{"r":"19","cells":["","","","Draft liability total","=#REF!  [缓存: 缺失]","Prior review roll-forward"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Personnel Support","row_count":9,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Personnel support extract"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Current as supplied by People Operations."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Employee Ref","Employment Support","Payment / Settlement Evidence","Evidence Date","Support Source"]},{"r":"5","cells":["E001","Confirmed","No payment/settlement evidence","2024-07-10","Payroll support extract"]},{"r":"6","cells":["e002 ","Confirmed","No payment/settlement evidence","2025-02-01","Payroll support extract"]},{"r":"7","cells":["E003","Confirmed","No payment/settlement evidence","2024-10-10","Payroll support extract"]},{"r":"8","cells":["E004","Confirmed","Paid in full","2025-07-05","Payment register PR-774"]},{"r":"9","cells":["E005","Confirmed","Settled","2025-07-12","Settlement memo SM-22"]},{"r":"10","cells":["E007","Confirmed","No payment/settlement evidence","2025-07-20","Payroll support extract"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/orrindale_compliance_assessment.docx","bytes":38363,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a878dabe9898541da86c73d2962446f1946b9083d44b63cfd7c1e3608e565c15.docx","sha256":"a878dabe9898541da86c73d2962446f1946b9083d44b63cfd7c1e3608e565c15","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Orrindale Engineering — California Wage Liability Assessment\nMeasurement date: 30 June 2025 | Prepared for Ibrahim Boateng | Review response to Aleksy Rosenthal\nConclusion\nRecognized California liability is $2,650.00 for 3 unique supported claims, measured at 30 June 2025. Unresolved California claimed exposure is $1,550.00 (2 claims: C-1006 and C-1009); these amounts are not recognized because personnel support is incomplete, not because the claims are settled. Nevada claim C-1003 ($700.00), paid/settled California claims C-1004 ($500.00) and C-1005 ($900.00), duplicate row C-1008 ($1,200.00), and post-measurement C-1007 ($300.00) are excluded from the recognized total.\nBasis and Jurisdiction Comparison\nThe claims table was identified at Claims Export!D6:K16; the adjacent M:N office-metrics table was excluded. Employee keys were matched case-insensitively after trimming terminal spaces. California claims on or before 30 June 2025 with no explicit payment or settlement evidence are recognized at the claimed gross wage. C-1001 is retained once and C-1008 is linked as its duplicate. C-1004 and C-1005 are excluded only because personnel support explicitly says “Paid in full” and “Settled.”\nPeriod comparison (same recognized population): 2024 recognized $1,200.00; 2025 recognized $1,450.00; increase $250.00. The 2025 amount comprises C-1002 ($850.00) and C-1010 ($600.00). Slash dates are interpreted MM/DD/YYYY; therefore 05/06/2025 is 6 May 2025. This is a disclosed convention for the ambiguous date.\nThe supplied guidance snapshot states that California scope is distinct from Nevada, explicit payment/settlement evidence supports exclusion, administrative status alone is insufficient, unsupported records remain unresolved, and later dates are outside the measurement population. Nevada C-1003 is shown for comparison only and does not affect the California total.\nExceptions and Assumptions\nC-1006 ($450.00) and C-1009 ($1,100.00) have no personnel support row. Their combined $1,550.00 is unresolved claimed exposure; recognized amount is blank/non-recognized in the workbook. C-1008 duplicates C-1001 by normalized employee key, date, category, and amount, so its amount is not multiplied. Raw statuses are preserved; Due/Open/Outstanding/Unpaid are treated as claim indicators, while Paid/Settled require explicit support. No penalties, interest, or unsupported adjustments are included.\nSource References\n1. orrindale_wage_claims_source.xlsx, Claims Export!D6:K16 (claims and source notes), Personnel Support!A4:E10 (employment and payment/settlement evidence). 2. california_nevada_wage_guidance.docx, “California treatment,” “Nevada comparison,” and “Measurement boundary and amounts” paragraphs. Source files were retained unchanged.\nChange Log\nReview issue\nResponse\nRecords/evidence\nDuplicate employee rows\nNormalized and grouped; recognized once with lineage.\nC-1001/C-1008\nStatus labels\nRaw labels retained; semantic interpretation disclosed.\nAll claims; E004/E005\nMixed dates\nCanonical dates added; MM/DD/YYYY convention disclosed.\nC-1005/C-1008/C-1010\nStale calculation\nReference-error draft quarantined; totals recomputed.\nSource draft and Liability sheet","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/orrindale_wage_workpaper.xlsx","bytes":11699,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/8eb01fdfdbce793f5cc17b3c3837f2c0fc8b70063f2c231f7f7eac4961451695.xlsx","sha256":"8eb01fdfdbce793f5cc17b3c3837f2c0fc8b70063f2c231f7f7eac4961451695","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Source Trace","row_count":12,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Source Trace — claims table identified at Claims Export!D6:K16; side table M:N excluded"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Claim ID","Raw Employee Ref","Normalized Employee Key","Jurisdiction","Raw Date","Canonical Date","Wage Category","Claimed Gross Wage","Raw Status","Personnel Evidence","Disposition","Recognized Amount","Duplicate Group","Reason / Source Fact"]},{"r":"3","cells":["C-1001","E001","E001","California","2024-06-30","45473","Regular wages","1200","Due","No payment/settlement evidence","Recognized California liability","1200","C-1001","In-scope, on/before measurement date, no payment/settlement evidence"]},{"r":"4","cells":["C-1002","E002","E002","California","2025-01-15","45672","Overtime","850","Open","No payment/settlement evidence","Recognized California liability","850","C-1002","In-scope, on/before measurement date, no payment/settlement evidence"]},{"r":"5","cells":["C-1003","E003","E003","Nevada","2024-09-30","45565","Regular wages","700","Due","No payment/settlement evidence","Excluded — Nevada comparison only","","C-1003","Jurisdiction outside California scope"]},{"r":"6","cells":["C-1004","E004","E004","California","2025-06-30","45838","Bonus","500","Paid","Paid in full","Excluded — explicit payment/settlement","","C-1004","Paid in full evidence in personnel support"]},{"r":"7","cells":["C-1005","E005","E005","California","2025/06/30","45838","Regular wages","900","Settled","Settled","Excluded — explicit payment/settlement","","C-1005","Settled evidence in personnel support"]},{"r":"8","cells":["C-1006","E006","E006","California","2025-06-30","45838","Overtime","450","Due","No support row","Unresolved — unsupported personnel record","","C-1006","No personnel support row; absence is not settlement evidence"]},{"r":"9","cells":["C-1007","E007","E007","California","2025-07-15","45853","Regular wages","300","Due","No payment/settlement evidence","Excluded — after measurement date","","C-1007","Earning date is after 30 June 2025"]},{"r":"10","cells":["C-1008","E001 ","E001","California","06/30/2024","45473","Regular wages","1200","Outstanding","No payment/settlement evidence","Duplicate — linked to C-1001","","C-1001 / C-1008","Same normalized employee, date, category and amount as C-1001"]},{"r":"11","cells":["C-1009","E008","E008","California","2023-12-31","45291","Regular wages","1100","Unpaid","No support row","Unresolved — unsupported personnel record","","C-1009","No personnel support row; absence is not settlement evidence"]},{"r":"12","cells":["C-1010","e002","E002","California","05/06/2025","45783","Overtime","600","Due","No payment/settlement evidence","Recognized California liability","600","C-1010","In-scope, on/before measurement date, no payment/settlement evidence"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Liability","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Recognized California liability (30 June 2025 measurement)"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Claim ID","Normalized Employee Key","Canonical Date","Period","Claimed Gross Wage","Recognized Amount","Disposition","Source Trace Link",""]},{"r":"3","cells":["C-1001","E001","45473","2024","1200","1200","Recognized California liability","Source Trace!A3"]},{"r":"4","cells":["C-1002","E002","45672","2025","850","850","Recognized California liability","Source Trace!A4"]},{"r":"5","cells":["C-1010","E002","45783","2025","600","600","Recognized California liability","Source Trace!A12"]},{"r":"6","cells":[]},{"r":"7","cells":["Total recognized California liability","","","","","2650","","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":[]},{"r":"9","cells":["Period comparison","Recognized amount","Change vs prior period"]},{"r":"10","cells":["2024","1200",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["2025","1450","250"]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Exceptions","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Exceptions and excluded / unresolved population"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Claim ID","Jurisdiction","Canonical Date","Claimed Amount","Disposition","Recognized Amount","Reason","Personnel Evidence","Duplicate Group"]},{"r":"3","cells":["C-1003","Nevada","45565","700","Excluded — Nevada comparison only","","Jurisdiction outside California scope","No payment/settlement evidence","C-1003"]},{"r":"4","cells":["C-1004","California","45838","500","Excluded — explicit payment/settlement","","Paid in full evidence in personnel support","Paid in full","C-1004"]},{"r":"5","cells":["C-1005","California","45838","900","Excluded — explicit payment/settlement","","Settled evidence in personnel support","Settled","C-1005"]},{"r":"6","cells":["C-1006","California","45838","450","Unresolved — unsupported personnel record","","No personnel support row; absence is not settlement evidence","No support row","C-1006"]},{"r":"7","cells":["C-1007","California","45853","300","Excluded — after measurement date","","Earning date is after 30 June 2025","No payment/settlement evidence","C-1007"]},{"r":"8","cells":["C-1008","California","45473","1200","Duplicate — linked to C-1001","","Same normalized employee, date, category and amount as C-1001","No payment/settlement evidence","C-1001 / C-1008"]},{"r":"9","cells":["C-1009","California","45291","1100","Unresolved — unsupported personnel record","","No personnel support row; absence is not settlement evidence","No support row","C-1009"]},{"r":"10","cells":["","","","","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["Unresolved claimed exposure","","","1550","Not recognized; support incomplete","","Sum of unsupported California claims C-1006 and C-1009","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Method","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Method and review responses"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Topic","Applied treatment"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Population","Only rows in Claims Export!D6:K16 identified by claim headers are claims. The unrelated M:N table is excluded."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Key normalization","Employee keys are joined on UPPER(TRIM(raw key)); raw keys remain in Source Trace."]},{"r":"5","cells":["Duplicates","C-1001 and C-1008 share normalized key E001, date, category and amount. C-1001 is retained once; C-1008 is duplicate with full lineage."]},{"r":"6","cells":["Status interpretation","Due, Open, Outstanding and Unpaid are treated as claim indicators only. Paid/Settled labels are not sufficient alone; explicit personnel evidence is required."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Dates","ISO and slash dates are canonicalized to YYYY-MM-DD. Slash forms are interpreted MM/DD/YYYY; 05/06/2025 is flagged as an ambiguous convention and consistently treated as 6 May 2025."]},{"r":"8","cells":["Measurement date","California claims dated on or before 30 June 2025 are considered; later dates are excluded from this measured population."]},{"r":"9","cells":["Recognition","Recognized amount equals claimed gross wage with no penalties, interest or other additions. Unsupported claims remain blank/non-recognized."]},{"r":"10","cells":["Jurisdiction","California is measured; Nevada records are comparison-only and excluded from California total."]},{"r":"11","cells":["Stale calculation","The source draft reference-error calculation was quarantined and not used. All totals are recomputed from claim-level rows."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Change Log","row_count":6,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Change Log"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Review issue","Response in revised package","Affected records / evidence"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Duplicate employee rows","Normalized key and grouped duplicate; recognized once with lineage.","C-1001 and C-1008"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Inconsistent status labels","Retained raw labels and disclosed semantic interpretation; explicit payment support controls exclusion.","All claims; E004/E005 support"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Mixed date conventions","Added raw and canonical dates; applied MM/DD/YYYY to slash forms and flagged 05/06/2025 assumption.","C-1005, C-1008, C-1010"]},{"r":"6","cells":["Stale calculation","Quarantined source reference-error draft calculation; recomputed claim-level totals.","Source draft; Liability total"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted workbook is present under the exact requested filename and is a readable XLSX file.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filesystem and workbook-open inspection.","grader_hint":"Confirm the filename, extension, and that the workbook opens without corruption."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted assessment is present under the exact requested filename and is a readable DOCX file.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filesystem and document-open inspection.","grader_hint":"Confirm the filename, extension, and that the document opens and contains extractable text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains the five requested worksheet names: `Source Trace`, `Liability`, `Exceptions`, `Method`, and `Change Log`.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook sheet-name inspection.","grader_hint":"Check exact names, including spaces and capitalization."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every source claim that affects the conclusion is represented in the workbook with a source identifier, original claimed amount, source date or period, jurisdiction, and disposition.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compare the source workbook’s claim population with `Source Trace`, `Liability`, and `Exceptions`.","grader_hint":"Reconcile source claim identifiers to the delivered trace. No claim may vanish merely because it was excluded or unresolved."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered source trace identifies the actual claims table despite the banner and gutter columns and does not treat banner or gutter text as claim records.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compare source coordinates and extracted records.","grader_hint":"Inspect the original workbook’s non-A1 table placement and verify that only the real claims table feeds the analysis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The unrelated table beside the claims table is excluded from all liability totals, record counts, joins, and conclusions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Trace formulas, source identifiers, and population reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Confirm that values or labels from the side table do not appear as claim rows or affect any aggregate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Join matching treats employee keys that differ only by case or trailing whitespace as the same key, while retaining the original key for traceability.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reperform joins against the source claims and personnel support records.","grader_hint":"Normalize case and terminal whitespace independently and verify that equivalent keys resolve to one employee identity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Duplicate claim rows are identified and do not cause the same underlying wage claim to be counted more than once.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspect duplicate grouping, source identifiers, and liability aggregation.","grader_hint":"Use the source claim attributes and employee-key normalization to test that repeated underlying claims are collapsed or otherwise prevented from double counting."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each duplicate treatment preserves lineage to all relevant source rows and explains why the recognized amount is not multiplied by the repeated records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Source Trace`, `Exceptions`, and method narrative.","grader_hint":"A reviewer should be able to move from a retained claim to every duplicate source row and understand the disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Inconsistent raw status labels are mapped or interpreted consistently, with the mapping or judgment disclosed rather than silently replacing the source labels.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Raw status values, delivered classification fields, and `Method` or `Exceptions` notes.","grader_hint":"Check that semantically equivalent labels receive a consistent treatment and that ambiguous labels are not silently normalized away."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A claim with explicit support for payment or settlement is excluded from recognized California liability, with the source support and exclusion reason shown.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compare the guidance, personnel support extract, and claim disposition.","grader_hint":"Verify the exclusion is based on explicit supplied evidence rather than on a label alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A claim lacking personnel support is not presented as settled solely because the support is absent; its unresolved status and effect on the conclusion are visible.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Exceptions`, `Method`, and the assessment narrative.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear unresolved or unsupported disposition and confirm that no unsupported settlement fact is asserted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For records whose support is insufficient to recognize an amount, the recognized-liability field is left blank or otherwise explicitly non-recognized rather than filled with an estimate or a misleading zero.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claim-level output and exception treatment.","grader_hint":"Inspect unresolved rows specifically; distinguish a documented non-recognition state from an invented estimate or an assertion that nothing is owed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The unresolved claimed exposure reported in the workbook equals the sum of source claim amounts assigned to the unresolved or unsupported population, within ±$0.01.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Exceptions` amounts reconciled to source claims.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from the source amounts using the delivered unresolved population and compare with the reported exposure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recognized liability population includes only claims within the California scope stated in the supplied guidance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction fields, claim classifications, and guidance citation.","grader_hint":"Reperform the jurisdiction filter and verify that the population definition is stated in both artifacts or clearly linked between them."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Records governed by the supplied Nevada comparison are not included in the California liability total and are visibly identified as out of scope or comparison-only.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Liability`, `Exceptions`, and jurisdiction comparison section.","grader_hint":"Check both the aggregate and the row-level disposition for non-California records."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The as-of-date population follows the measurement-date treatment in the supplied guidance, with pre-measurement claims considered and later claims not silently included.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Canonical dates, period fields, dispositions, and guidance citation.","grader_hint":"Test boundary and later-dated records against the stated measurement-date rule."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"ISO and slash-form source dates are parsed into a consistent canonical representation while the original date text remains traceable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Source Trace` original and normalized date fields.","grader_hint":"Compare each raw date format with its normalized counterpart and verify that no date was silently dropped."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The assessment makes a defensible, reproducible choice for ambiguous slash-form dates, states the assumption, and explains any resulting sensitivity or exception.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Method`, `Exceptions`, and `Assumptions` section of the DOCX.","grader_hint":"Accept a professionally defensible convention if it is explicit, consistently applied, and its effect is addressed; do not require an unstated house convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each recognized claim amount equals the supportable source wage amount after the delivered inclusion, duplicate, jurisdiction, and as-of-date classifications, within ±$0.01.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Claim-level source-to-output reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Recalculate recognized amounts from the supplied source and verify that no unsupported adjustment, penalty, interest, or conversion has been introduced."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook’s recognized California liability total equals the sum of its recognized claim amounts, within ±$0.01.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Liability` detail and total.","grader_hint":"Reperform the aggregation from the delivered claim-level recognized population."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The period comparison uses the same recognized-population definition as the overall California liability and does not count duplicate, Nevada, settled, or unresolved records as recognized amounts.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period fields, claim dispositions, and comparison table or narrative.","grader_hint":"Recalculate each period from the claim-level classification and compare the included population with the overall total."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The period totals and the reported change between periods are arithmetically consistent with the claim-level recognized amounts, within ±$0.01.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Liability` period comparison and assessment narrative.","grader_hint":"Recalculate period totals and the stated absolute or directional change; accept the stated presentation if the arithmetic and labels agree."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook and assessment respond to the duplicate-row, status-label, date, and stale-calculation review comments with a disposition or documented unresolved judgment for each.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Change Log`, `Method`, `Exceptions`, and review-response text in the DOCX.","grader_hint":"Map each supplied review issue to a concrete response; a generic statement that the file was reviewed is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stale calculation error in the supplied workbook is not propagated into the deliverables, and the correction or quarantine is documented in the change log.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Comparison with the source workbook and delivered `Change Log`.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the old erroneous calculation is neither used as an input nor left unexplained in the revised workpaper."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The method note states the population definition, duplicate treatment, key normalization, status interpretation, date convention, unresolved-record treatment, and amount calculation sufficiently for independent recomputation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"The `Method` sheet and corresponding assessment passages.","grader_hint":"Check for operationally specific explanations tied to the supplied records, not merely general assertions of compliance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment’s California and Nevada comparison accurately reflects the supplied guidance and distinguishes comparison context from the California measurement conclusion.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Guidance document, `Basis and Jurisdiction Comparison`, and workbook references.","grader_hint":"Compare each stated jurisdictional distinction with the supplied guidance and verify that Nevada facts do not alter the California total."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All material exclusions have a reason tied to a source fact or the supplied guidance, and the excluded amount or population effect is quantified where an amount exists.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"`Exceptions` and assessment exceptions section.","grader_hint":"Inspect exclusions for explicit source-based reasons and reconcile their amounts to the source population."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook and assessment cite or identify both supplied source files and preserve enough source identifiers for a reviewer to locate the underlying record or guidance passage.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source references, source IDs, and guidance citations.","grader_hint":"Verify that references are usable offline and are not generic claims that unnamed materials were consulted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package is review-ready: a second analyst can trace a claim, understand its disposition, reproduce the totals, and distinguish recognized, excluded, and unresolved exposure without relying on oral explanation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and DOCX viewed together.","grader_hint":"Judge navigability, labeling, cross-references, and whether the presentation supports actual frontline execution without sacrificing audit traceability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment presents facts and supported conclusions without adding recommendations, unsupported legal assertions, invented settlement facts, or unprovided personnel facts.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full DOCX text and workbook narrative fields.","grader_hint":"Compare factual claims with the supplied files and verify that the requested fact-presenting authority has been respected."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recognized California liability, unresolved exposure, and period comparison figures shared by the workbook and assessment agree within ±$0.01.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-deliverable comparison of shared metrics.","grader_hint":"Extract every shared amount from both artifacts and compare both value and population label; do not accept agreement achieved by ambiguous labels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook and assessment use the same definitions for recognized, excluded, and unresolved populations and do not present contradictory conclusions about any material claim group.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-document comparison of classifications, totals, and narrative.","grader_hint":"Sample claim groups and compare the row-level workbook disposition with the corresponding assessment explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Neither deliverable contains spreadsheet error tokens such as `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!`, or `#VALUE!` in visible or formula-result content.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook formula/value scan and DOCX text extraction.","grader_hint":"Scan cell values, formulas, cached results, and extracted document text for the specified error strings."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"You are an auditor at Granthill Press reviewing a compliance workpaper for Orrindale Engineering. The package will be used by a frontline employee to trace claim-level support and understand the California liability conclusion.","difficulty_sources":["Finding the real claims table when a banner, gutter columns, and a neighboring unrelated table are present","Normalizing case- and whitespace-variant employee keys without losing original source lineage","Distinguishing duplicate claims, explicit settlement evidence, and unsupported personnel records","Interpreting inconsistent statuses and mixed or ambiguous date forms under a supplied jurisdictional guidance snapshot","Producing dependent claim-level, period, exception, and cross-document outputs that reconcile to one another"],"authoring_plan":{"source_files":{"workbook":{"semantic_contents":"Create a synthetic but internally coherent claims workbook for a regional engineering employer. The real claims table must contain claim identifiers, employee reference keys, jurisdiction, earning date or period, wage category, claimed gross wage, raw status, and source notes. Include a separate personnel-support extract that can establish employment and payment or settlement evidence for some claims. Include records spanning multiple periods, California and Nevada jurisdictions, at least one record outside the measurement-date population, duplicate underlying claims, and a claim whose personnel support is absent or insufficient. Use explicit source evidence to distinguish a settled claim from an unresolved claim; do not make absence of a support row mean settlement.","required_imperfections":["Place a non-data banner block above the real claims table and blank gutter columns to its left so the claims table does not begin at A1.","Place an unrelated table beside the real claims table on that same worksheet. Give one header in that unrelated table an embedded line break.","Vary employee join keys only by case and trailing whitespace across the claims and personnel-support data.","Include inconsistent raw status labels that require a disclosed semantic interpretation.","Mix ISO-form and slash-form dates, including at least one genuinely ambiguous slash-form date whose interpretation should be disclosed.","Include a stale draft calculation containing a reference error that is not a valid source fact and must not feed the revised result."],"avoid":["Do not introduce additional layout defects such as hidden rows, hidden worksheets, broken external links, merged data cells, truncated headers, corrupted files, or unrelated formula errors.","Do not put any graded answer only in an image or other non-text-extractable object.","Do not make duplicate amounts or source records internally contradictory; the ambiguity should concern interpretation and support, not corrupted arithmetic."]},"guidance_document":{"semantic_contents":"Create a plausible internal compliance guidance snapshot issued for use at the measurement date. It must contain the governing treatment for California wage claims and a comparison section for Nevada, including the scope of due and unpaid wages, treatment of explicit payment or settlement evidence, handling of duplicate or unsupported claims, jurisdictional scope, and the measurement-date boundary. It should clarify that administrative status labels alone are not settlement evidence and that unresolved support must remain distinguishable from a conclusion that no liability exists. It may state that the workpaper excludes penalties and interest. The guidance must be sufficiently extractable and citeable offline, but must not prescribe the solver's spreadsheet layout or provide a purpose-built answer table."}},"transformation_and_gold":{"normalization":"The reference solution identifies the actual claims table by its headers and position rather than assuming the upper-left worksheet cell. It trims terminal whitespace and normalizes case for employee-key joins while retaining raw keys. It parses both date styles into canonical dates, flags the ambiguous date, and applies a documented convention consistently.","classification":"The gold classifies each claim using the supplied guidance and source evidence: supported in-scope California claims are recognized once; explicit settlement or payment evidence is excluded; Nevada records are comparison-only and excluded from the California total; duplicate underlying claims are grouped with complete lineage; unsupported claims remain visibly unresolved and do not receive an invented recognized amount; later-than-measurement claims are outside the measured population. Status labels are recorded in raw and interpreted forms.","calculations":"A reference script derives recognized claim amounts, total California liability, period totals, period change, excluded amounts, and unresolved exposure directly from the authored source workbook and the guidance-defined classifications. It never hard-codes a gold total. Shared figures in the workbook and DOCX are generated from the same derived result object and rounded consistently to cents.","review_artifacts":"The gold workbook preserves a traceable source representation, records the unrelated-table exclusion, documents normalization and date assumptions, lists every material exclusion and unresolved item, and logs the stale formula correction or quarantine. The gold assessment explains the conclusion, period movement, California/Nevada comparison, unresolved exposure, source references, and responses to the review comments without recommendations.","validation":"Use offline spreadsheet and DOCX libraries plus a reference script to recalculate every claim classification and aggregate. Scan both deliverables for spreadsheet error tokens, compare all shared figures and population definitions, and render both files for a professional usability review. Confirm that every rubric item is achievable from the two supplied reference files without internet access."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"wage_claim_source_workbook","filename":"orrindale_wage_claims_source.xlsx","purpose":"Contains the claim transaction population, personnel support extract, source identifiers, dates, jurisdiction fields, status labels, claimed wage amounts, and the original draft calculation that must be reviewed.","required":true,"discovery":"Inspect the workbook structure before calculating anything. The claim table is not positioned at the upper-left corner, and an unrelated table is present on the same worksheet."},{"artifact_id":"jurisdiction_guidance_snapshot","filename":"california_nevada_wage_guidance.docx","purpose":"A supplied internal compliance guidance snapshot current at the measurement date. It states the California and Nevada treatment relevant to due, paid or settled, unsupported, duplicate, out-of-scope, and as-of-date wage claims.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this supplied guidance as the governing source for the jurisdiction comparison and cite the relevant passages in the assessment."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"revised_workpaper","filename":"orrindale_wage_workpaper.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A review-ready calculation workbook with source traceability, claim-level classification, recognized California liability, period comparison, exclusions, unresolved exposure, method notes, and a change log.","required":true,"constraints":["Use exactly the sheets `Source Trace`, `Liability`, `Exceptions`, `Method`, and `Change Log`.","Preserve source identifiers and original source values sufficiently for a reviewer to trace every included, excluded, and unresolved record.","Do not include the unrelated side table in the liability population.","Do not overwrite or alter the supplied source workbook."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"compliance_assessment","filename":"orrindale_compliance_assessment.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise compliance assessment explaining the California conclusion, period changes, California and Nevada comparison, unresolved exposure, assumptions, source references, review responses, and changes made to the draft.","required":true,"constraints":["Use the headings `Conclusion`, `Basis and Jurisdiction Comparison`, `Exceptions and Assumptions`, `Source References`, and `Change Log`.","Present the same shared figures, population definitions, and conclusions as the workbook.","Present facts and supported conclusions only; do not recommend actions or invent unsupported legal, personnel, or settlement facts."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"analyze_data","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"accountants_auditors","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":6.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"Validate the source-derived classification and aggregates with an offline reference script, then have an independent reviewer inspect the rendered workbook and assessment for traceability, judgment disclosure, source support, and cross-deliverable consistency.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The supplied guidance snapshot is the offline authority for the jurisdiction comparison; no live legal research is required or permitted.","An ambiguous date may support more than one professionally defensible convention when the convention, sensitivity, and downstream effect are clearly disclosed."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:03:21+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:03:21+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:03:21+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-17T08:03:21+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/ab33f23fcf3fb266","declared_deliverables":["orrindale_wage_workpaper.xlsx","orrindale_compliance_assessment.docx"]};
